1
00:02:30,967 --> 00:02:37,507
This is the time known as the Great Pirate Era.

2
00:02:37,827 --> 00:02:41,827
A countless array of pirates go to battle across the seas in search of the One Piece,

3
00:02:42,067 --> 00:02:46,007
the legendary treasure left behind by Gold Roger, King of the Pirates.

4
00:02:46,487 --> 00:02:50,887
Makini Luffy, a boy whose body turned to rubber after eating the gum-gum fruit,

5
00:02:51,187 --> 00:02:53,647
set sail to become the next King of the Pirates.

6
00:02:54,027 --> 00:02:56,627
As Luffy and his crew conquer numerous obstacles,

7
00:02:56,927 --> 00:02:59,747
they capture the unwanted attention of the world government,

8
00:02:59,747 --> 00:03:02,847
which will use any means necessary to stop them.

9
00:03:04,087 --> 00:03:05,527
This sight!

10
00:03:06,587 --> 00:03:09,387
Can't wait to see what kind of adventure's up next!

11
00:03:10,127 --> 00:03:13,167
With a charted course awash in danger and intrigue,

12
00:03:13,387 --> 00:03:17,447
the crew will cut a path across the Grand Line to the New World.

13
00:03:20,467 --> 00:03:25,227
Luffy was sent flying from the Sabaody Archipelago by Bartholomew Kuma.

14
00:03:26,227 --> 00:03:28,547
After soaring through the sky for hours,

15
00:03:28,547 --> 00:03:31,827
he found himself in a kingdom inhabited entirely by women.

16
00:03:32,427 --> 00:03:34,447
Its name was Amazon Lily.

17
00:03:36,927 --> 00:03:38,527
Everyone falls in love!

18
00:03:38,887 --> 00:03:40,307
Pirate Empress Hancock!

19
00:03:40,307 --> 00:03:57,567
Sorry I can't pay you back for saving my life and stuff,

20
00:03:57,687 --> 00:04:00,247
but I got places to go and a crew that's waiting for me!

21
00:04:00,687 --> 00:04:02,887
And that means bye-bye, Lady Land!

22
00:04:02,887 --> 00:04:06,187
Men truly are mysterious.

23
00:04:06,767 --> 00:04:09,607
Their arms stretch, they grow fat without warning,

24
00:04:09,987 --> 00:04:12,867
their chests are flat, and between their legs they have...

25
00:04:12,867 --> 00:04:13,367
Ugh!

26
00:04:13,367 --> 00:04:13,867
Ugh!

27
00:04:13,867 --> 00:04:17,427
I hate to ask you for your help again, but could you take these off for me?

28
00:04:17,507 --> 00:04:18,267
Your family jewels?

29
00:04:18,267 --> 00:04:19,647
Would you drop it?

30
00:04:19,647 --> 00:04:21,347
I mean these things!

31
00:04:21,787 --> 00:04:23,907
I said I was going to see my friends, remember?

32
00:04:24,147 --> 00:04:26,847
If I show up looking like this, they're all gonna laugh at me!

33
00:04:26,847 --> 00:04:31,847
I think they look nice, but I suppose...

34
00:04:31,847 --> 00:04:32,687
There.

35
00:04:33,187 --> 00:04:34,307
Hey, thanks, Lady!

36
00:04:34,547 --> 00:04:35,407
You're the best!

37
00:04:36,667 --> 00:04:39,067
I can't imagine anyone hating frills.

38
00:04:39,447 --> 00:04:41,027
You men are just too strange.

39
00:04:41,767 --> 00:04:43,927
Yeah, well, whatever you say.

40
00:04:44,067 --> 00:04:45,827
Either way, thanks for taking them off.

41
00:04:46,367 --> 00:04:48,307
Okay, bye for real this time.

42
00:04:48,487 --> 00:04:49,147
I gotta hurry.

43
00:04:49,727 --> 00:04:51,227
Are all men so hasty?

44
00:04:51,227 --> 00:04:58,327
I can't rest till I know my friends survive like I did.

45
00:04:58,447 --> 00:04:59,467
That's all that matters.

46
00:05:00,847 --> 00:05:02,587
Because as long as they're alive,

47
00:05:03,127 --> 00:05:05,987
we can get back up and keep fighting!

48
00:05:14,167 --> 00:05:16,667
I'm gonna get stronger than all those guys!

49
00:05:19,927 --> 00:05:21,067
Let's do this!

50
00:05:21,227 --> 00:05:23,907
I'll walk all the way back to Sabaody on my hands!

51
00:05:24,027 --> 00:05:25,487
That'll toughen me up for sure!

52
00:05:30,447 --> 00:05:32,007
Think you could give me a ship?

53
00:05:32,247 --> 00:05:34,487
Wow, you really are hasty.

54
00:05:35,067 --> 00:05:36,467
Do you have any ships?

55
00:05:36,867 --> 00:05:38,187
We're in a Calm Belt?

56
00:05:38,587 --> 00:05:39,367
That's right.

57
00:05:39,867 --> 00:05:42,267
This island lies in an area known as a Calm Belt,

58
00:05:42,587 --> 00:05:44,967
and it's surrounded by a giant den of sea canes.

59
00:05:45,787 --> 00:05:48,807
That's another reason sailors never dare to come near this place.

60
00:05:48,807 --> 00:05:51,487
Castaways do sometimes make their way to our shores,

61
00:05:51,487 --> 00:05:53,487
but they almost always do so as corpses.

62
00:05:53,987 --> 00:05:57,027
Wait, but you said your leader was part of a pirate crew, right?

63
00:05:57,147 --> 00:05:59,027
The ship of our snake princess, the Yuta,

64
00:05:59,107 --> 00:06:01,327
is pulled by two giant poisonous sea snakes,

65
00:06:01,407 --> 00:06:03,647
so even sea kings don't dare to attack it.

66
00:06:03,647 --> 00:06:06,207
And it's the only ship on Amazon Lily.

67
00:06:09,327 --> 00:06:10,527
This sucks!

68
00:06:10,867 --> 00:06:12,007
And there's no wind?

69
00:06:12,247 --> 00:06:14,707
Should I just build a raft and paddle all the way there?

70
00:06:16,407 --> 00:06:17,667
That's a joke, right?

71
00:06:18,327 --> 00:06:18,867
Hey!

72
00:06:18,987 --> 00:06:21,107
I'll just build a raft and paddle all the way there!

73
00:06:21,107 --> 00:06:22,187
Wait, you weren't joking?

74
00:06:27,707 --> 00:06:28,147
Yeah!

75
00:06:28,827 --> 00:06:29,707
It died!

76
00:06:30,527 --> 00:06:32,047
But it's already falling apart!

77
00:06:37,167 --> 00:06:37,987
What's wrong?

78
00:06:38,167 --> 00:06:40,487
He said he was a pirate, but he can't even swim?

79
00:06:40,487 --> 00:07:03,927
I had no obligation to save you.

80
00:07:04,427 --> 00:07:06,647
Do all men sink like a rock even if they're sailors?

81
00:07:06,647 --> 00:07:12,667
That was close.

82
00:07:12,907 --> 00:07:13,727
Damn it!

83
00:07:14,367 --> 00:07:16,007
If only Frankie was here!

84
00:07:16,647 --> 00:07:17,567
I'm screwed!

85
00:07:18,007 --> 00:07:19,907
You're not the only one with problems!

86
00:07:21,487 --> 00:07:23,047
Why did you have to cling to me

87
00:07:23,047 --> 00:07:24,807
when you should have been running away from here?

88
00:07:36,647 --> 00:07:46,787
If this keeps up much longer,

89
00:07:46,887 --> 00:07:48,447
I'll end up growing attached to you!

90
00:07:49,487 --> 00:07:50,367
Hold on!

91
00:07:50,587 --> 00:07:51,327
Just stop!

92
00:07:54,247 --> 00:07:55,987
Why do you want to shoot me?

93
00:07:55,987 --> 00:08:10,347
You know, come to think of it,

94
00:08:10,387 --> 00:08:12,067
these arrows are crazy strong!

95
00:08:12,687 --> 00:08:14,247
When those girls were chasing me earlier,

96
00:08:14,327 --> 00:08:16,547
they were busting up stone walls with those things!

97
00:08:17,247 --> 00:08:19,727
Doesn't look like there's anything special about them, though!

98
00:08:20,667 --> 00:08:22,747
Well, of course these arrows are strong.

99
00:08:22,867 --> 00:08:23,947
They're imbued with our hockey.

100
00:08:23,947 --> 00:08:25,927
You're mocking me, aren't you?

101
00:08:26,167 --> 00:08:26,687
Hockey?

102
00:08:27,387 --> 00:08:28,607
I never heard of it.

103
00:08:29,407 --> 00:08:30,427
There she is!

104
00:08:31,107 --> 00:08:32,127
Margaret, are you safe?

105
00:08:34,447 --> 00:08:35,547
You made it!

106
00:08:35,727 --> 00:08:36,567
The man's with her!

107
00:08:36,647 --> 00:08:37,547
Strike him down!

108
00:08:39,147 --> 00:08:39,627
Coward!

109
00:08:42,807 --> 00:08:43,767
Come back!

110
00:08:44,267 --> 00:08:45,747
Forgive me if you were injured, Margaret,

111
00:08:45,847 --> 00:08:47,407
but our situation is quite dire.

112
00:08:47,647 --> 00:08:48,847
The Snake Princess has returned,

113
00:08:48,927 --> 00:08:51,027
so we must vanquish this fiend post-haste!

114
00:08:51,027 --> 00:08:51,267
Huh?

115
00:08:51,267 --> 00:08:51,327
Huh?

116
00:08:53,947 --> 00:09:08,547
You're quite bold to lay your anchor

117
00:09:08,547 --> 00:09:10,007
in Sea King-infested waters,

118
00:09:10,307 --> 00:09:11,507
unless you're just fools.

119
00:09:14,287 --> 00:09:17,707
Yes, we did notice the Sea Kings, thank you.

120
00:09:17,707 --> 00:09:20,647
The Sea Prism Stone on this battleship

121
00:09:20,647 --> 00:09:23,367
may conceal our presence from the beasts for a while,

122
00:09:23,767 --> 00:09:25,367
but after waiting here for so long,

123
00:09:25,667 --> 00:09:27,587
they eventually caught on and attacked us.

124
00:09:28,107 --> 00:09:30,307
We would prefer to avoid such encounters,

125
00:09:30,787 --> 00:09:31,887
but as you know,

126
00:09:32,147 --> 00:09:34,307
the agreement between the Kuja and the government

127
00:09:34,307 --> 00:09:35,907
forbids us from getting closer

128
00:09:35,907 --> 00:09:37,927
than three kilometers from your island.

129
00:09:38,887 --> 00:09:40,027
So, like fools,

130
00:09:40,207 --> 00:09:41,887
here we are waiting in a monster's nest

131
00:09:41,887 --> 00:09:44,087
while you ladies take your sweet time.

132
00:09:44,087 --> 00:09:45,847
Hey, have you heard?

133
00:09:46,007 --> 00:09:47,527
They say that the ruler of the Kuja

134
00:09:47,527 --> 00:09:49,667
is a monster that can turn people to stone.

135
00:09:49,867 --> 00:09:50,647
That's stupid.

136
00:09:51,427 --> 00:09:52,687
You killed that Sea King?

137
00:09:52,847 --> 00:09:54,287
Well, you can color me impressed.

138
00:09:57,587 --> 00:09:59,667
Those of us who travel on the Grand Line

139
00:09:59,667 --> 00:10:01,427
are no strangers to these creatures,

140
00:10:02,027 --> 00:10:03,567
but the ones here in the Calm Belt

141
00:10:03,567 --> 00:10:06,547
are certainly larger and decidedly more ferocious.

142
00:10:06,547 --> 00:10:16,527
Any sign of the Kuja's ship?

143
00:10:16,767 --> 00:10:18,747
Uh, no, not yet, Vice Admiral.

144
00:10:19,087 --> 00:10:20,907
No approaching ships anywhere in sight.

145
00:10:23,187 --> 00:10:25,347
How long does she intend to keep us waiting?

146
00:10:25,707 --> 00:10:27,867
Or perhaps the Empress has changed her mind?

147
00:10:27,867 --> 00:10:39,227
It's a Sea King!

148
00:10:40,447 --> 00:10:40,947
Fire!

149
00:10:41,407 --> 00:10:41,927
Fire!

150
00:10:51,507 --> 00:10:52,387
No way!

151
00:10:52,727 --> 00:10:54,787
Our cannons didn't even leave a mark on that thing!

152
00:10:54,787 --> 00:11:01,767
The whole ship's gonna be smashed to pieces

153
00:11:01,767 --> 00:11:03,007
if we don't do something quick!

154
00:11:03,387 --> 00:11:04,887
Yeah, but what can we do?

155
00:11:05,327 --> 00:11:06,607
We gave it all we had!

156
00:11:11,727 --> 00:11:14,127
That thing isn't gonna eat the whole ship, is it?

157
00:11:17,127 --> 00:11:19,247
I had hope for a greeting from the Empress,

158
00:11:19,367 --> 00:11:20,107
not this monster!

159
00:11:20,427 --> 00:11:23,027
However, I shall meet it all the same!

160
00:11:23,027 --> 00:11:48,727
Look, guys!

161
00:11:49,287 --> 00:11:50,087
He's alive!

162
00:11:50,087 --> 00:11:53,307
Monster though it may be,

163
00:11:53,387 --> 00:11:55,787
if I allowed that beast to devour a marine vessel!

164
00:11:56,667 --> 00:11:58,727
How could I call myself a Vice Admiral?

165
00:11:59,087 --> 00:12:09,327
What strange marks?

166
00:12:09,507 --> 00:12:11,167
Did you cut from the inside of its stomach?

167
00:12:11,167 --> 00:12:14,147
I am not here to hunt Sea Kings or to chat about them.

168
00:12:14,667 --> 00:12:16,127
Let us conduct our business quickly

169
00:12:16,127 --> 00:12:17,667
so that I may leave these waters.

170
00:12:21,347 --> 00:12:23,527
Your words are as sharp as your blade.

171
00:12:25,007 --> 00:12:27,647
Then hear them well, Kuja Pirates!

172
00:12:27,807 --> 00:12:29,307
I tire of waiting here.

173
00:12:29,307 --> 00:12:33,807
I am Vice Admiral Momonga of Navy Headquarters,

174
00:12:33,887 --> 00:12:35,607
Warlord of the Sea,

175
00:12:35,727 --> 00:12:37,827
and Pirate Empress Boa Hancock!

176
00:12:37,947 --> 00:12:39,607
I have come for you!

177
00:12:40,067 --> 00:12:40,947
Reveal yourself!

178
00:12:41,607 --> 00:12:44,547
The Snake Princess does not cater to your beck and call.

179
00:12:44,647 --> 00:12:45,527
There's your answer.

180
00:12:45,647 --> 00:12:47,107
You might as well go home now.

181
00:12:47,107 --> 00:12:48,727
Look at those ugly men!

182
00:12:48,907 --> 00:12:50,447
Unsophisticated force!

183
00:12:50,487 --> 00:12:52,527
I haven't seen a live one in a long time!

184
00:12:52,727 --> 00:12:56,087
Whenever pirates or merchants see the Kuja flag flying above the island,

185
00:12:56,247 --> 00:12:57,227
they play in terror!

186
00:12:58,527 --> 00:13:00,627
That laugh isn't very ladylike.

187
00:13:00,907 --> 00:13:02,587
We received a message from your princess.

188
00:13:02,947 --> 00:13:04,927
She claimed that she would reply to our summons,

189
00:13:04,927 --> 00:13:07,307
but now it appears she was not quite sincere.

190
00:13:08,807 --> 00:13:10,207
This morning's paper,

191
00:13:10,847 --> 00:13:12,407
a place and date has been decided

192
00:13:12,407 --> 00:13:14,827
for the public execution of Portgus D. Ace,

193
00:13:14,967 --> 00:13:17,427
the Second Division Commander of the Whitebeard Pirates.

194
00:13:17,667 --> 00:13:19,247
There is no turning back now.

195
00:13:19,967 --> 00:13:22,167
The world government has issued strict orders

196
00:13:22,167 --> 00:13:24,107
that the seven warlords of the sea assemble,

197
00:13:24,547 --> 00:13:26,827
refuse, and our agreement will become void,

198
00:13:27,227 --> 00:13:30,587
and your princess's title as warlord will be revoked.

199
00:13:31,167 --> 00:13:32,627
Think about that for a moment.

200
00:13:33,007 --> 00:13:34,707
Until now, you have done as you please

201
00:13:34,707 --> 00:13:35,727
just because of your position.

202
00:13:36,107 --> 00:13:38,667
But if you are unwilling to grant us this favor,

203
00:13:38,947 --> 00:13:41,607
you will be reduced to nothing but ordinary pirates,

204
00:13:42,027 --> 00:13:43,667
which means you'll be adversaries

205
00:13:43,667 --> 00:13:46,027
of the Marines and world government alike.

206
00:13:46,487 --> 00:13:47,847
Do you hear me?

207
00:13:48,427 --> 00:13:49,607
Boa Hancock!

208
00:14:04,847 --> 00:14:06,347
Boa Hancock!

209
00:14:06,347 --> 00:14:06,987
Boa Hancock!

210
00:14:07,107 --> 00:14:07,827
Boa time!

211
00:14:07,967 --> 00:14:08,527
Boa Hancock!

212
00:14:08,527 --> 00:14:09,667
Boa Hancock!

213
00:14:09,827 --> 00:14:10,667
Boa Hancock!

214
00:14:10,667 --> 00:14:14,247
Boa Hancock!

215
00:14:14,427 --> 00:14:15,487
Boa Hancock!

216
00:14:15,727 --> 00:14:16,407
Boa Hancock!

217
00:14:16,507 --> 00:14:17,767
Boa Hancock!

218
00:14:17,767 --> 00:14:19,247
Boa Hancock!

219
00:14:19,407 --> 00:14:22,087
Boa Hancock!

220
00:14:22,267 --> 00:14:22,947
Boa Hancock!

221
00:14:23,827 --> 00:14:26,327
Boa Hancock!

222
00:14:26,327 --> 00:14:26,747
Boa Hancock!

223
00:14:26,747 --> 00:14:27,967
Boa Hancock!

224
00:14:28,187 --> 00:14:28,827
Boa Hancock!

225
00:14:29,067 --> 00:14:29,487
Boa Hancock!

226
00:14:29,507 --> 00:14:30,147
Boa Hancock!

227
00:14:30,367 --> 00:14:31,147
Boa Hancock!

228
00:14:31,147 --> 00:14:32,547
Boa Hancock!

229
00:14:32,547 --> 00:14:52,947
Which one of you had the audacity to place this kitten in my path?

230
00:14:55,427 --> 00:14:59,087
My deepest apologies, Empress. I accept full responsibility.

231
00:14:59,707 --> 00:15:01,167
You should be more careful.

232
00:15:01,167 --> 00:15:03,787
Yes, of course. Stop it.

233
00:15:04,227 --> 00:15:06,367
At long last, Bower Hancock.

234
00:15:19,847 --> 00:15:21,787
Careful, men. Keep your guard up.

235
00:15:21,787 --> 00:15:26,487
The Vice Admiral is right. I'm still not convinced those women aren't really monsters in disguise.

236
00:15:27,027 --> 00:15:29,887
There's no telling how frightening their leader could be. Brace yourselves!

237
00:15:31,167 --> 00:15:41,387
That's the pirate empress?

238
00:15:41,727 --> 00:15:43,607
She's the most beautiful woman in the world.

239
00:15:43,607 --> 00:15:58,667
Crap! Crap! Crap!

240
00:15:58,667 --> 00:16:02,727
Crap! Crap! Crap!

241
00:16:05,727 --> 00:16:08,007
Halt, man! Face me!

242
00:16:08,627 --> 00:16:11,367
Oh, jeez. The girls from this island are scary as heck.

243
00:16:11,627 --> 00:16:13,607
I'll take Nami over them any day.

244
00:16:13,607 --> 00:16:18,647
Well, maybe not.

245
00:16:24,787 --> 00:16:26,907
That's what those crazy arrows that I've done for!

246
00:16:27,587 --> 00:16:27,867
There!

247
00:16:27,947 --> 00:16:28,887
Crap! Crap!

248
00:16:28,987 --> 00:16:30,107
All right, here goes!

249
00:16:30,107 --> 00:16:30,947
Here goes!

250
00:16:40,847 --> 00:16:43,727
This fiend behaves more like a monkey than a human man.

251
00:16:43,727 --> 00:16:45,427
Dammit, what are we going to do?

252
00:16:45,427 --> 00:16:47,287
We cannot allow him to run free here,

253
00:16:47,287 --> 00:16:48,847
not with the Empress coming.

254
00:16:48,847 --> 00:16:50,727
We have no choice but to hunt him down

255
00:16:50,727 --> 00:16:52,467
and kill him as quickly as possible.

256
00:16:53,387 --> 00:16:55,287
Our time is short, we must split up.

257
00:16:55,287 --> 00:16:58,427
Very well, may your arrows find their target, my sisters.

258
00:16:58,427 --> 00:16:59,267
They shall.

259
00:17:00,947 --> 00:17:03,187
Maybe it's not a good idea to go this way.

260
00:17:03,187 --> 00:17:06,267
I mean, this is where I was running away from before.

261
00:17:06,267 --> 00:17:08,227
Oh, it'll work out.

262
00:17:08,227 --> 00:17:10,727
I can always run back to the jungle if I have to.

263
00:17:10,727 --> 00:17:11,567
Up there!

264
00:17:11,567 --> 00:17:13,187
No, no!

265
00:17:13,187 --> 00:17:15,147
I won't miss my mark this time.

266
00:17:20,287 --> 00:17:21,167
Is he dead?

267
00:17:21,167 --> 00:17:22,007
Not yet.

268
00:17:22,007 --> 00:17:24,007
The man just slipped and fell into the jungle.

269
00:17:30,107 --> 00:17:40,447
So you've come for me at last.

270
00:17:43,347 --> 00:17:45,147
Stubborn and meddlesome, I see.

271
00:17:47,147 --> 00:17:48,247
I shall be frank.

272
00:17:48,247 --> 00:17:50,547
I have no intention of keeping my promise.

273
00:17:50,547 --> 00:17:53,887
In other words, I refuse to go to war for you.

274
00:17:55,507 --> 00:17:58,387
Still, I rather like my position as a warlord.

275
00:17:58,607 --> 00:18:00,367
So, I think I shall keep it.

276
00:18:04,127 --> 00:18:08,587
Also, you shall give me all the cargo on your ship quickly without complaint.

277
00:18:08,587 --> 00:18:09,667
That's enough.

278
00:18:09,667 --> 00:18:13,667
I won't stand for you acting like a spoiled child.

279
00:18:13,667 --> 00:18:17,667
Do you honestly think we'll accept such unreasonable demands?

280
00:18:21,667 --> 00:18:22,667
Haul it over, men!

281
00:18:22,667 --> 00:18:23,667
Huh?

282
00:18:23,667 --> 00:18:25,667
I'll do anything you want.

283
00:18:25,667 --> 00:18:27,667
Order me around some more.

284
00:18:27,667 --> 00:18:30,667
Put that cargo down this instant or I'll throw you overboard!

285
00:18:30,667 --> 00:18:31,667
Oh, sorry.

286
00:18:31,667 --> 00:18:32,667
I couldn't resist her, sir.

287
00:18:36,667 --> 00:18:40,667
Porkas Deace's public execution will be exactly one week from today.

288
00:18:41,667 --> 00:18:44,667
The event will be held in the town square of Marineford.

289
00:18:44,667 --> 00:18:47,667
In other words, we're doing this inside of Navy Headquarters itself.

290
00:18:48,667 --> 00:18:52,667
There is no doubt that Whitebeard will attempt to rescue him in the next few days.

291
00:18:52,667 --> 00:18:55,667
Likely with the strength of his entire crew behind him.

292
00:18:55,667 --> 00:19:00,667
Under the leadership of three admirals and with the aid of the seven warlords of the sea,

293
00:19:00,667 --> 00:19:03,667
Navy Headquarters is determined to stop him at any cost.

294
00:19:04,667 --> 00:19:07,667
Will you give up the title of warlord or accept your orders?

295
00:19:08,667 --> 00:19:09,667
Make your decision quickly.

296
00:19:09,667 --> 00:19:11,667
You've kept us waiting long enough!

297
00:19:22,667 --> 00:19:24,667
I already told you I like being a warlord.

298
00:19:24,667 --> 00:19:27,667
However, I loathe the world government.

299
00:19:27,667 --> 00:19:30,667
I have no interest in following their orders.

300
00:19:30,667 --> 00:19:33,667
Surely I can find a better solution.

301
00:19:34,667 --> 00:19:36,667
Oh, I know. How does this sound?

302
00:19:37,667 --> 00:19:40,667
The Marines who came to escort me had a mysterious accident.

303
00:19:40,667 --> 00:19:45,667
When they were discovered, they had all been transformed into stone and were promptly disposed of.

304
00:19:45,667 --> 00:19:49,667
She's planning to do something. Don't let your guard down!

305
00:19:49,667 --> 00:19:51,667
I've heard about Hancock doing this before.

306
00:19:51,667 --> 00:19:56,667
A merchant ship was attacked by the Kuja pirates and when it was discovered later, there weren't any crew members on board.

307
00:19:56,667 --> 00:19:58,667
Just a bunch of weird statues.

308
00:19:58,667 --> 00:20:07,667
Hey! Look at that! Those aren't people, are they?

309
00:20:08,667 --> 00:20:11,667
You mean they were all turned to stone?

310
00:20:11,667 --> 00:20:17,667
I've had enough of these threats. Your temper tantrums will not be tolerated, do you hear me?

311
00:20:17,667 --> 00:20:24,667
Our big sister has a rotten personality. But in the end, she always gets her way.

312
00:20:24,667 --> 00:20:28,667
Indeed. And there's a very good reason for that.

313
00:20:28,667 --> 00:20:43,667
Would you like to know why? Because no matter what I do, even if I kick a kitten, even if I yank off your ears.

314
00:20:45,667 --> 00:20:54,667
Why, even if I were to commit murder, the world would forgive me. And that is because, yes, it is because I am beautiful.

315
00:20:58,667 --> 00:21:06,667
You're right! You can abuse me all you want, your highness!

316
00:21:06,667 --> 00:21:08,667
Stop that, you fools!

317
00:21:14,667 --> 00:21:21,667
The guilty thoughts swimming in your hearts shall turn your flesh to stone.

318
00:21:25,667 --> 00:21:27,667
Love, love be.

319
00:21:28,667 --> 00:21:49,667
Oh, I'd expect no less from a Navy Vice Admiral. Clever. Forcing the wicked thoughts from your mind with pain.

320
00:21:50,667 --> 00:21:56,667
I do applaud your conviction. Though, I can't extend that compliment to your men.

321
00:21:57,667 --> 00:21:58,667
They should be ashamed.

322
00:21:59,667 --> 00:22:01,667
Now you're the only one left.

323
00:22:01,667 --> 00:22:02,667
But one, is not zero.

324
00:22:02,667 --> 00:22:06,667
But one, is not zero.

325
00:22:06,667 --> 00:22:07,667
Is not zero.

326
00:22:07,667 --> 00:22:08,667
Is not zero.

327
00:22:08,667 --> 00:22:30,667
What?

328
00:22:30,667 --> 00:22:34,667
We shall return to our peaceful home of Amazon Lily.

329
00:22:34,667 --> 00:22:36,667
Aye, aye, Snake Princess!

330
00:22:39,667 --> 00:22:42,667
Listen up, Boa Hancock! I won't turn away!

331
00:22:42,667 --> 00:22:44,667
I refuse to return empty-handed!

332
00:22:44,667 --> 00:22:47,667
Unless you reappear in two days,

333
00:22:47,667 --> 00:22:50,667
your position will be revoked.

334
00:22:50,667 --> 00:23:00,667
Do as you wish.

335
00:23:06,667 --> 00:23:08,667
Luffy storms the Kuja village

336
00:23:08,667 --> 00:23:10,667
in hopes of acquiring a boat,

337
00:23:10,667 --> 00:23:12,667
but accidentally lands in a bath

338
00:23:12,667 --> 00:23:14,667
where Empress Hancock is bathing.

339
00:23:14,667 --> 00:23:16,667
As he peers through the steam,

340
00:23:16,667 --> 00:23:18,667
rising from its waters,

341
00:23:18,667 --> 00:23:21,667
sees a forbidden secret etched upon her back.

342
00:23:21,667 --> 00:23:23,667
On the next, One Piece!

343
00:23:23,667 --> 00:23:25,667
The secret hidden on the backs!

344
00:23:25,667 --> 00:23:27,667
Luffy and the Snake Princess meet!

345
00:23:27,667 --> 00:23:29,667
I'm gonna be king of the pirates!

